</code></pre> <p>Real output:</p> <pre><code>[ERROR] Low: Inconsistent synchronization of com.playbook.tools.InconsistentCache.size; locked 83% of time
        Unsynchronized access at InconsistentCache.java:[line 29]
        Synchronized access at InconsistentCache.java:[line 24] ... [line 19] ... [line 15]  IS2_INCONSISTENT_SYNC
</code></pre> <p>Lesson learned while writing this page: set the threshold to Low</p> <p>With the common <code>&lt;threshold&gt;Medium&lt;/threshold&gt;</code>, SpotBugs reported nothing for this real bug. <code>IS2_INCONSISTENT_SYNC</code> is a heuristic ("locked 83% of time"), and it's ranked Low priority. For concurrency checks, run with <code>threshold=Low</code> and filter to <code>MT_CORRECTNESS</code> (as <code>spotbugs-mt-only.xml</code> does) to keep the noise down.</p> <p>Other SpotBugs MT patterns: <code>DC_DOUBLECHECK</code>, <code>JLM_JSR166_UTILCONCURRENT_MONITORENTER</code> (synchronizing on a <code>ReentrantLock</code> object), <code>SWL_SLEEP_WITH_LOCK_HELD</code>, <code>UL_UNRELEASED_LOCK</code>, <code>NN_NAKED_NOTIFY</code>, <code>WA_NOT_IN_LOOP</code>, <code>STCAL_INVOKE_ON_STATIC_DATE_FORMAT_INSTANCE</code>, <code>AT_NONATOMIC_OPERATIONS_ON_SHARED_VARIABLE</code>.</p>

Java 8 — bounded poolJava 21 — thread per connection <pre><code>ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(200);   // max 200 concurrent clients
try (ServerSocket server = new ServerSocket(9000)) {
    while (true) {
